VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED

The field rename, the `luhn` extraction into a shared private primitive, `locality` delegating to the new `regionOf`, and the audit/event/schema/OpenAPI updates are all coherent and idiomatic. One structural issue remains:

**Duplicated memberId-parsing loop across `regionOf` and `fiscalYear(String)`** (`Owner.java:683-692` and `Owner.java:831-844`). Both methods independently re-implement the identical "skip the leading run of letters" scan to locate the end of the REGION segment:

```java
int i = 0;
while (i < memberId.length() && Character.isLetter(memberId.charAt(i))) {
    i++;
}
```

Each now encodes its own copy of the knowledge that "REGION is the leading letters, and the FY segment starts right after them." That is the same `memberId` layout parsed in two places; if the format ever shifts, both loops must change in lockstep. This is exactly the kind of duplication the unification was meant to avoid — note `locality` was correctly collapsed to delegate to `regionOf`, but `fiscalYear(String)` was not given the same treatment.

Suggested fix: extract a single private helper that returns the region-segment boundary (the index after the leading letters), e.g.:

```java
private static int regionEnd(String memberId) {
    int i = 0;
    while (i < memberId.length() && Character.isLetter(memberId.charAt(i))) {
        i++;
    }
    return i;
}
```

Then have `regionOf` build its result from `regionEnd(...)` (`i == 0 ? "UNKNOWN" : memberId.substring(0, i)`) and have `fiscalYear(String)` read `start = regionEnd(memberId)` instead of its own loop. That keeps the memberId's segment layout defined in exactly one place, matching how `locality`/`regionOf` already share.

